TITLE Equilibration with Pure Phases of Gypsum and Anhydrite

SOLUTION 1 Aqueous species of the fluid
    units mol/kgw
    Na 0.03
    K 0.01
    Ca 1e-5
    Mg 1e-7
    Cl 0.025
    Fe 1e-7
    pH 7
    temp 25.0 # Celcius

EQUILIBRIUM_PHASES 1 Equilibrium calculation (steady-state)
    Gypsum      0.0 1.0     # Saturation Index; Amount in mol
    Anhydrite   0.0 1.0     # Saturation Index; Amount in mol

REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1 Reaction temperature you can control
    25.0 75.0 in 51 steps

USER_GRAPH 1
    -headings       Temperature Gypsum Anhydrite
    -chart_title    "Gypsum-Anhydrite Stability"
    -axis_scale     x_axis  25 75 5 0
    -axis_scale     y_axis  auto 0.05 0.1
    -axis_titles    "Temperature, degC" "Saturation Index"
    -initial_solutions false
    -start
    10 graph_x TC
    20 graph_y SI("Gypsum") SI("Anhydrite")
    -end

END